1
00:00:00,822 --> 00:00:03,940
A receipt is only the start of a reimbursement.

2
00:00:04,327 --> 00:00:07,187
 Small teams still need to check the evidence, apply

3
00:00:07,187 --> 00:00:10,348
 their policy, approve the expense, and track

4
00:00:10,348 --> 00:00:10,822
 the payment.

5
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:15,580
Carry brings those steps into one traceable workflow.

6
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:18,420
 This walkthrough uses synthetic receipts

7
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:21,500
 and simulated extraction and payments so you

8
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:24,636
 can explore the working application without credentials.

9
00:00:26,005 --> 00:00:28,050
Alex submits a travel expense.

10
00:00:28,183 --> 00:00:31,094
 The receipt stays beside its extracted

11
00:00:31,094 --> 00:00:33,561
 details, making the evidence easy to

12
00:00:33,561 --> 00:00:34,338
 inspect.

13
00:00:34,716 --> 00:00:37,738
 Alex reviews the amount, confirms the expense

14
00:00:37,738 --> 00:00:40,850
 and payment evidence, and submits the claim.

15
00:00:41,027 --> 00:00:43,938
 The reimbursement recipient is confirmed separately in

16
00:00:43,938 --> 00:00:44,583
 their profile.

17
00:00:50,889 --> 00:00:53,976
Carry checks the claim against explicit reimbursement

18
00:00:53,976 --> 00:00:54,671
 rules.

19
00:00:55,063 --> 00:00:58,106
 Missing evidence and policy exceptions remain visible

20
00:00:58,302 --> 00:01:00,932
 with reasons the applicant and reviewer can

21
00:01:00,932 --> 00:01:01,802
 inspect.

22
00:01:02,063 --> 00:01:05,128
 AI output is treated as evidence to confirm.

23
00:01:05,345 --> 00:01:08,367
 Deterministic application rules control routing.

24
00:01:11,138 --> 00:01:14,094
Morgan, the finance reviewer, checks the original

25
00:01:14,094 --> 00:01:16,783
 receipt and records an approval reason.

26
00:01:16,961 --> 00:01:19,694
 That approval belongs to this claim version,

27
00:01:20,072 --> 00:01:22,338
 amount, policy, and recipient.

28
00:01:22,516 --> 00:01:25,605
 The decision history preserves what was reviewed

29
00:01:25,605 --> 00:01:26,827
 and why it was approved.

30
00:01:32,997 --> 00:01:35,476
Approval and payment are separate steps.

31
00:01:35,845 --> 00:01:38,845
 Morgan confirms the exact amount and recipient

32
00:01:38,845 --> 00:01:41,345
 before starting the simulated payment.

33
00:01:41,823 --> 00:01:43,736
 Processing does not mean paid.

34
00:01:44,041 --> 00:01:46,910
 Carry synchronizes the individual payment result

35
00:01:46,910 --> 00:01:48,823
 before updating its status.

36
00:01:49,019 --> 00:01:51,889
 The implemented PayPal Sandbox adapter

37
00:01:51,889 --> 00:01:54,606
 follows this payment intent and reconciliation flow.

38
00:01:57,916 --> 00:01:59,294
Now consider a blurry,

39
00:02:00,272 --> 00:02:01,583
 420-pound receipt.

40
00:02:01,938 --> 00:02:04,494
 Carry requests better evidence.

41
00:02:04,761 --> 00:02:07,694
 A clearer replacement resolves the evidence issue,

42
00:02:07,916 --> 00:02:10,783
 but the expense still exceeds the example policy

43
00:02:10,783 --> 00:02:13,627
 limit and requires finance review.

44
00:02:13,894 --> 00:02:16,605
 Better evidence does not remove the policy

45
00:02:16,605 --> 00:02:17,116
 exception.

46
00:02:20,879 --> 00:02:24,066
Carry combines receipt evidence, explicit rules,

47
00:02:24,212 --> 00:02:26,587
 human review, and payment tracking.

48
00:02:26,837 --> 00:02:29,608
 Real AI calls and PayPal Sandbox transactions

49
00:02:29,941 --> 00:02:31,358
 remain to be verified.

50
00:02:31,462 --> 00:02:34,462
 The working local demo and MIT licensed source are

51
00:02:34,462 --> 00:02:35,441
 available today.

52
00:02:35,754 --> 00:02:38,462
 Carry, from receipt to reimbursement, with every

53
00:02:38,462 --> 00:02:39,350
 decision explained.